@startuml
' Source of truth for 04-key-management.png -- see ../README.md to regenerate.
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
title Where the per-file data key is protected

rectangle "Per-file DEK\nRAND_bytes in the BE" as DEK
rectangle "key_metadata =\nStandardKeyMetadata(DEK + aad_prefix)\nDEK IS IN THE CLEAR" as KM

DEK --> KM

rectangle "Iceberg metadata-encryption chain (Iceberg >= 1.11)" as CHAIN {
  rectangle "manifest\nAES-GCM stream, AGS1 magic\nholds each data file's key_metadata" as M1
  rectangle "manifest list\nAES-GCM stream, AGS1 magic\nholds each manifest's key + AAD prefix" as M2
  rectangle "manifest-list key metadata\nencrypted with a KEK\nAAD = KEK creation timestamp" as M3
  rectangle "metadata.json (NOT encrypted)\nencryption-keys: KEK wrapped by\nthe table master key\nsnapshot.key-id = KEK_ID" as M4
  M1 --> M2 : key recovered from
  M2 --> M3 : key recovered from
  M3 --> M4 : KEK recovered from
}

KM --> M1 : carried in

rectangle "KMS\ntable master key" as KMS
M4 --> KMS : the ONLY KMS call\nper KEK, not per file

note right of KM
  This is why the dependency floor is Iceberg 1.11.0 and not a
  preference: without the chain below, the same code leaves a
  usable key in cleartext storage beside the file it decrypts.
end note

note bottom of CHAIN
  StarRocks implements none of this chain -- Iceberg does.
  StarRocks contributes the data-file layer plus carrying
  key_metadata across the FE<->BE boundary.
  The KEK rotates per NIST SP 800-57; previous KEKs are
  retained for existing snapshots.
end note
@enduml
